  "caveat": "Software-rendered WebGL (SwiftShader) on a shared 4-CPU container with no GPU, under heavy load from other jobs. Frame intervals and absolute times understate real hardware and never prove smoothness. JavaScript self time by owner (CPU profile), render submission per frame, renderer counts and heap are the closest hardware-independent signals. Long tasks come from the page's longtask observer; selfTimeMs.browserNative is native browser work outside JavaScript (with software WebGL this includes waiting on the rasterizing GPU process), so a long task without matching JavaScript self time is not script work. scriptPerFrameMs buckets top-level script events between frame starts and overstates the tail when frames are sparse. Real-GPU and device smoothness must be confirmed by a person on that hardware.",
  "notes": {
    "programs": "Linked shader programs come from the stand-in's extra programs field; the contract's stats do not include programs yet.",
    "renderSubmissionMs": "The environment's own frame times: the duration of each renderer.render call over the most recent rendered frames (up to 120)."
  }
}
